<p>Two kinds of helper live here. <strong>Ghost's</strong> are modelled by <code>site/lib/ghost.mjs</code> so every partial renders in the docs exactly as it will in a theme; <strong>the docs' own</strong> exist only on this site. The utilities are Tailwind <code>@utility</code> rules, so they take variants (<code>md:im-stack</code>).</p>

<h2>Helpers modelled</h2>
<p>{{helpers.length}} names, read from the registry at build time.</p>
<div class="im-cluster" style="--im-cluster-gap: .375rem">{{#each helpers}}<code>{{"{{"}}{{this}}{{"}}"}}</code>{{/each}}</div>

<h2>A field must not share a helper's name</h2>
<p>An ambiguous <code>{{"{{price}}"}}</code> resolves to the helper, not the field, and prints nonsense. The build names any fixture field a helper shadows; the four that legitimately read their own field — <code>excerpt</code>, <code>reading_time</code>, <code>url</code>, <code>content</code> — are allowed.</p>

<h2>Docs-only helpers</h2>
<div class="im-table-scroll"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Helper</th><th></th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code>{{"{{icon \"name\"}}"}}</code></td><td>An icon partial by name. In a theme write <code>{{"{{> \"icons/name\"}}"}}</code>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>{{"{{#example}}"}}</code></td><td>A preview plus its source, emitted <em>between</em> prose blocks. <code>spill=true</code>, <code>flush=true</code>, <code>code=false</code>, <code>center=true</code>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>{{"{{{{code \"lang\"}}}}"}}</code></td><td>A raw block that prints Handlebars without running it.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>{{"{{#match a op b}}"}}</code></td><td>Ghost's, extended: <code>= != &gt; &lt; &gt;= &lt;= ~ ~^ ~$</code>.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

